Artwork notice

The MIT license covers the theme palette and documentation.
It does not relicense the historical artwork in backgrounds/ or preview.png.

Artwork: Wang Ximeng, A Thousand Li of Rivers and Mountains (1113), ink and
color on silk. Collection: The Palace Museum, Beijing.

The wallpaper crops derive from Wikimedia Commons reproductions.
"A Thousand Li of Rivers and Mountains Section 1.jpg" (Dale1 stolaf)
is dedicated under CC0 1.0. The "1c Wang Ximeng..." and "1e Wang Ximeng..."
sections (Eugene a) are identified by Commons as public-domain artwork and
faithful PD-Art reproductions. See README.md for the exact source links and
rights statements. No ownership of the historical painting is claimed.
